  "sourceLocator": {
    "chapter": "Playing the Game",
    "section": "1.16",
    "heading": "Difficulty Class",
    "lineStart": 176,
    "lineEnd": 178
  },
  "section": "1.16",
  "rulesText": "The Difficulty Class for a saving throw is determined by the effect that causes it or by the GM. For example, if a spell forces you to make a save, the DC is determined by the caster's spellcasting ability and Proficiency Bonus. Monster abilities that call for saves specify the DC."
}
